---
import DesignSystemShell from "../../layouts/DesignSystemShell.astro";
import DsSection from "../../components/design-system/DsSection.astro";
import DsRule from "../../components/design-system/DsRule.astro";
import DsSpec from "../../components/design-system/DsSpec.astro";

// Small-multiples demo data: four offices, 13 weeks of expected receipts (sample values).
const offices = [
  { name: "Denver", weeks: [42, 38, 51, 47, 60, 55, 49, 62, 58, 44, 40, 52, 57] },
  { name: "Fort Collins", weeks: [18, 22, 20, 25, 19, 27, 30, 24, 21, 26, 28, 23, 25] },
  { name: "Dallas", weeks: [30, 28, 35, 41, 39, 33, 45, 48, 42, 37, 36, 44, 46] },
  { name: "Wichita", weeks: [8, 11, 9, 14, 12, 10, 15, 13, 9, 11, 16, 12, 14] },
];
const max = Math.max(...offices.flatMap((o) => o.weeks));
const spark = (w: number[]) => w.map((v, i) => `${(i / (w.length - 1)) * 120},${28 - (v / max) * 26}`).join(" ");
---

<DesignSystemShell slug="dashboards" source="docs/40-dashboard-design-system.md · app/command-center/src/scripts/executive-pipeline.ts">
  <DsSection id="tufte" title="Tufte's principles, applied">
    <p>
      Edward Tufte's rules for statistical graphics are the operating rules for every board and dashboard in the Command
      Center. Each principle below is paired with the concrete decision that enforces it here, so "Tufte" is a checklist,
      not a mood.
    </p>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Principle</th><th>What it means</th><th>How this app does it</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Maximise the data-ink ratio</strong></td><td>Every drop of ink should carry data; erase non-data ink and redundant data ink.</td><td>Borders, not shadows. No gridlines behind a table. Zebra rows only on boards where the eye must track across nine columns. No chart frames, no 3D, no gradients except the meter's blue→navy.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Avoid chartjunk</strong></td><td>Decoration that competes with the data.</td><td>Colour is never decorative (docs/40): every colour on a board encodes status. Icons never carry status. No illustrations on work surfaces.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Show the data</strong></td><td>The reader should be able to see the actual numbers.</td><td>The table is the primary chart. Every chart has a data table beside or beneath it; every KPI shows its number, not a gauge.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Small multiples</strong></td><td>Many small, same-scale panels beat one large chart with many series.</td><td>The Territory Map's per-office KPI cards; the 13-week cash map as a strip of same-height cells; per-office groups on WIP with identical columns and shared column-group state.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Layering and separation</strong></td><td>Use the least visual weight that still separates.</td><td>Ink hierarchy: 800 values, 400 body, muted 11px labels. One accent (gold) for attention. The one flag red for the one action.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Micro/macro readings</strong></td><td>Detail on inspection, pattern at a glance.</td><td>Expand-tree: office → branch → invoice → line, rolled-up progress at every level; ten rows per pane so the macro reading survives.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Integrity: label the units, show the denominator</strong></td><td>No lie factor; the graphic's proportions match the numbers.</td><td>Count lines state the denominator ("5 of 12"); compact axis ticks; zero coverage is "—" not "0%"; Review (UOM) instead of a fabricated variance; negative is a credit memo, never a payable.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Sparklines</strong></td><td>Word-sized graphics beside the number they describe.</td><td>Sanctioned for trend-beside-number on executive cards (below). Never as the only representation.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Don't dequantify</strong></td><td>Words like "high" and colours alone are not data.</td><td>Pills carry a word and a number where one exists ("Overdue 60d+ · $18,420"); lights carry a word and a time.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="shapes" title="Page shapes">
    <p>Four shapes cover every surface. Pick one; do not blend two on a page.</p>
    <div class="ds-grid-2">
      <div class="ds-card"><p class="eyebrow">Shape A · Work board</p><h3>Toolbar → KPI row → grouped ten-row panes</h3><p>Friday WIP/AR, the cash family, credit memos. Full-bleed, working density, both modes, one board-local primary. KPIs are filters. Groups are offices (or vendor → branch), each a ten-row pane with show-more.</p></div>
      <div class="ds-card"><p class="eyebrow">Shape B · Audit tree</p><h3>Toolbar → 4 question cards → expand-tree</h3><p>Invoice Audit, Order Audit, Estimate Audit, Agreement Builder. Office → Branch → Invoice → Line with category sections; progress at every level; the four cards are claim it / chase it / pay it / fix it, each with one button.</p></div>
      <div class="ds-card"><p class="eyebrow">Shape C · Executive dashboard</p><h3>Window selector → KPI row → two charts → per-account bars → drill table</h3><p>Pipeline Review, Cash Runway, Fixed Costs. Reading density, one step larger type, compact currency, charts in fixed-height cards, zero-value rows hidden with a caption.</p></div>
      <div class="ds-card"><p class="eyebrow">Shape D · Map + rail</p><h3>Toolbar over map → marker popups → sticky detail rail</h3><p>Territory Map (home). Filter bar above the map, never hidden; the rail card and the popup are the same HTML; every popup KPI links to a pre-filtered board.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p>Everything else (department overviews, the agent monitor, this site) is a <strong>reading page</strong>: hero → metric grid → panels, on the content rail.</p>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="kpi-rules" title="KPI rows">
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Four to six cards, never more.</strong> Invoice Audit went from seven pills to four by grouping by the question the human is answering. A seventh card is a sign two of them are context.</li>
      <li><strong>Each card is a queue:</strong> a count or a sum, a one-line scope, and the one button that works it. A number that changes nothing the human does next is subtext, not a card.</li>
      <li><strong>Pipelines read as a direction</strong> ("51 → 32 → 3"), not three backlogs.</li>
      <li><strong>Coloured left edge per question</strong> (brand / yellow / green / grey) so the groups read apart at a glance; the edge never encodes severity.</li>
      <li><strong>A filtering card carries <code>aria-pressed</code></strong> and the toolbar shows the active filter with a clear control.</li>
      <li><strong>History-only trailing pills.</strong> A "Signed (7d)" pill obeys the filter bar but not the window selector; dropping a milestone fallback removed a fake $1.5M spike (2026-07-07).</li>
      <li><strong>Off-scope cards dim</strong> (<code>.iv-kpi-off</code>, opacity .62) rather than disappear when the scope excludes them.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="charts" title="Charts">
    <p>Charts are for shape and comparison; tables are for values. Chart.js is registered tree-shaken (bar, line, category and linear scales, tooltip, legend — about 60 KB). Every chart lives in a fixed-height card so <code>responsive + maintainAspectRatio:false</code> cannot grow it unboundedly.</p>
    <DsSpec label="Stacked bar, brand palette, white on-bar labels" code="executive-pipeline.ts CHART_PALETTE · afterDatasetsDraw labels" layout="block">
      <div style="display:grid;gap:6px;width:100%;max-width:560px;font-size:11px">
        {[["Denver", 62, 22], ["Dallas", 48, 30], ["Fort Collins", 35, 9], ["Wichita", 18, 14]].map(([n, a, b]) => (
          <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:90px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:center"><span style="color:var(--text-muted)">{n}</span><div style="display:flex;height:22px;border-radius:3px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--surface-alt)"><span style={`width:${Number(a)}%;background:#11133f;color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700`}>{`$${a}K`}</span><span style={`width:${Number(b)}%;background:#c22326;color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700`}>{Number(b) >= 12 ? `$${b}K` : ""}</span></div></div>
        ))}
        <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:4px"><span><i style="display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;background:#11133f;border-radius:2px;vertical-align:-1px"></i> Collected</span><span><i style="display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;background:#c22326;border-radius:2px;vertical-align:-1px"></i> AR outstanding</span><span style="margin-left:auto">labels skipped below 24px · 14px thickness · on $0</span></div>
      </div>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Small multiples with sparklines (sanctioned shape for trend-beside-number)" code="inline SVG, same scale, one hue" layout="block">
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));gap:12px;width:100%">
        {offices.map((o) => (
          <div style="display:grid;gap:4px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;background:var(--surface)"><span style="font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:600">{o.name} · 13 wk</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px"><strong style="font-size:22px;font-weight:800;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums">${o.weeks.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0)}K</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 120 30" width="120" height="30" role="img" aria-label={`${o.name} weekly expected receipts, 13 weeks`}><polyline points={spark(o.weeks)} fill="none" stroke="var(--info)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round" /><circle cx="120" cy={28 - (o.weeks[12] / max) * 26} r="2" fill="var(--primary)" /></svg></div><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:11px">last week ${o.weeks[12]}K</small></div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </DsSpec>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Palette</td><td><code>["#11133f", "#3b6b4c", "#0066cc", "#eaa221", "#c22326"]</code> — navy, hunter green, smart blue, gold, flag red. Series colours are semantic, not rotational: Collected = navy, AR outstanding = flag red (the at-risk segment).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Chart types</td><td>Stacked bar (horizontal for funnels, vertical for leaderboards, top 8 only), line for time series, sparkline for trend-beside-number. No pie, no donut, no gauge, no 3D, no area fills under lines.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Size</td><td>Card 280px, plot 220px, fixed. Legend at the bottom, 10px note above the plot naming the series.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Axes</td><td>Compact currency ticks ($5K · $50K · $500K · $1M); no decimal precision on an axis; gridlines <code>--border</code> only on the value axis.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Labels</td><td>White 700 11px Inter drawn on segments by a custom plugin (no datalabels dependency); skipped under 24px along the bar, 14px across it, and on $0. Text reads the raw value so it always matches the bar.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Tooltips</td><td>Compact currency, series name, category; never the only place a value lives.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Dark mode</td><td>Re-read tokens and redraw on theme change; navy series lifts to smart blue on dark.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Accessibility</td><td><code>role="img"</code> + <code>aria-label</code> stating the finding; the table beneath is the accessible alternative.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Doctrine</td><td>A change to what a chart measures (e.g. cash map basis billed AR → balance due) is flagged as a doctrine change, never shipped silently.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="table-rules" title="Tables as the primary chart">
    <ul>
      <li>Columns ordered by what the meeting talks about first: identity (job, client) → owner (office, rep) → money (contract, billed, balance) → time (expected) → action. Money columns adjacent so the eye subtracts.</li>
      <li>Identity columns freeze; money scrolls. Job # + client pinned left at 72px + name.</li>
      <li>Totals as an end row with a 2px rule; section rows in caps; a breach cell white-on-red.</li>
      <li>Column groups (billed / cost / margin) collapse by default and expand globally so every office table stays the same width.</li>
      <li>Never a 15-wide table: headline columns as pills in the summary row, the rest in a labelled detail grid.</li>
      <li>Derived figures are computed live (balance to pay), never stored, so they cannot drift from their inputs.</li>
      <li>Rows that leave a population are flagged (<code>stale_closeout</code>), never deleted, and reachable through their own pill.</li>
      <li>A row that needs a system fix is never mixed with one that needs a phone call — the board would look like 346 problems when it has 120.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="numbers" title="Number formatting">
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Context</th><th>Format</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Table money</td><td>2 decimals, thousands, tabular, right</td><td class="num" style="font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums">$12,480.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td>KPI money</td><td>Compact to 3 significant figures</td><td class="num">$1.48M · $66.9K · $942</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Axis</td><td>Compact, no decimals under $1M</td><td class="num">$500K</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Percent</td><td>0–1 decimal; "—" when the denominator is zero</td><td class="num">34% · 36.4% · —</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Counts</td><td>Integer; denominator stated</td><td>5 of 12 · (53 more)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Negative</td><td>Minus sign, error colour; never parentheses on screen</td><td class="num" style="color:var(--error)">−$1,240.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Variance</td><td>Signed %, tolerance pill beside it (Minor &lt; 3%, Moderate 3–6%, Major &gt; 6%); sub-nickel = In Tolerance</td><td class="num">+4.2% · Moderate</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Age</td><td>Days integer + d, chip tone by age</td><td>142d</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Time</td><td>Local, short, in the count slot</td><td>10:41 AM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Dates</td><td>Mon D in cells, Mon D, YYYY in prose, ISO in data</td><td>Sep 19 · Sep 19, 2026 · 2026-09-19</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="lights-rules" title="Status lights">
    <p>The runtime board (docs/109) is a dashboard of dashboards: one light per API, agent, scheduled job and feed, grouped by kind, worst light first, with the summary counts at the top. Its rules apply to any future health surface.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Colour thresholds derive from each item's cadence; the legend is rendered once from code, never hand-written.</li>
      <li>Every light has a word and a "last run / as of" time. Unknown is a state, not an absence.</li>
      <li>Paused = red; fresh-but-empty = yellow; not configured = yellow; a credential the app should hold but lacks caps at yellow.</li>
      <li>Third parties are judged by this app's own pings (200 = green), not by an external monitor.</li>
      <li>Board re-renders every 30s from the JSON endpoint; reveal state persists.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="dash-rules" title="Rules">
    <div class="ds-rules">
      <DsRule id="D-01" title="The table is the primary chart; every chart has a table; every KPI shows its number." source="Tufte 'show the data'; docs/40 §4">
        <p>No gauges, no dials, no donuts.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="D-02" title="Colour on a board encodes status only; ink that carries no data is removed." source="docs/40 §1 semantic colour law">
        <p>Borders over shadows, zebra only where nine columns must be tracked, no chart decoration.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="D-03" title="KPI rows are four to six work queues; a number that changes nothing the user does next is subtext." source="Chris 2026-06-17, 2026-08-09">
        <p>Pipelines read as a direction.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="D-04" title="Same scale, same columns, same order across every group on a page (small multiples)." source="friday-wip.astro:184-189 global column-group state">
        <p>The eye must be able to track a column down the page.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="D-05" title="State the denominator and the unit; show '—' for a zero denominator; never a fabricated number." source="docs/40 §7; executive-pipeline.ts:766; CONVENTIONS §10c">
        <p>"5 of 12", "Review (UOM)", "—".</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="D-06" title="Charts use the five-colour brand palette semantically, live in fixed-height cards, use compact ticks and on-bar labels with minimum-size guards." source="executive-pipeline.ts:278-334; global.css .epl-chart-*">
        <p>Bar, line, sparkline only.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="D-07" title="Money-first ordering: at-risk descending for groups, then date, then absolute variance for lines; categories by sort_order." source="invoice-audit.ts:552-634">
        <p>Never alphabetical for anything with a dollar on it.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="D-08" title="Charts and meters redraw on theme change and animate only on first render." source="Modes MD-07; Motion MO-05">
        <p>Comparison must not wait.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="D-09" title="A change to what a figure measures is a doctrine change: flag it to the human before shipping." source="context/memory/2026-08-21 cash-map basis">
        <p>Billed AR → Balance due was flagged, not slipped in.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="D-10" title="Every list loader paginates; a PostgREST page of exactly 1000 is a truncation, not a count." source="docs/40 §8; kpi-pills.ts:16-19">
        <p>A silent undercount on money is the worst dashboard bug there is.</p>
      </DsRule>
    </div>
  </DsSection>
</DesignSystemShell>
